  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Incoming delegation from Namibia to the World Hydrogen Summit</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The combi-track &quot;Green Hydrogen&quot; (GH2) aims to accelerate the development of GH2 economies in Namibia. A previously commissioned study has identified the water-GH2 connection as a key area for collaboration. Several Memoranda of Understanding (MoUs) have been signed between Dutch and Namibian organisations in this field.The World Hydrogen Summit, held in Rotterdam, presents an ideal platform to showcase the Dutch sector and allow companies to present their latest advancements. By inviting high-level delegates from Namibian organisations involved in the GH2 sector, the project aims to facilitate deeper cooperation between public and private entities from both countries. This serves the following objectives:&#x2022;	Positioning the Netherlands as a significant partner in the transition towards a green economy and ecosystem, thereby creating opportunities for Dutch businesses and innovations across the entire value chain, while also advancing development, sustainability, and climate agendas.&#x2022;	Collaborating with South Africa and Namibia to address their challenges and enhance the implementation of their plans regarding GH2.&#x2022;	Enhancing skills development initiatives through Dutch knowledge and technology transfer.In September, a follow-up mission to Namibia will be arranged, during which Dutch businesses and organisations will participate in the Global African Hydrogen Summit and engage in networking opportunities with local counterparts.</narrative>
  </description>
